# Tasks: AUTONOMY-POLICY

Purpose:
  Define the L0–L5 autonomy levels and project-level autonomy policy.
  The AI does NOT choose its autonomy level — it is determined by
  project policy. Autonomy decreases as risk increases: high-risk
  work always requires more human involvement regardless of the
  level assigned to a domain.

Owns:
  Autonomy levels L0–L5
  Project-level @policy.autonomy declarations
  Reversible vs irreversible action classification
  Risk level to authority mapping

AutonomyLevels:

  L0 — Observe Only
    description: AI may read and summarize, no actions
    authority: none
    actions: observe, report
    approval_required: all actions

  L1 — Suggest
    description: AI proposes changes, human executes
    authority: recommend only
    actions: propose code changes, propose tests
    approval_required: all changes

  L2 — Implement + Test
    description: AI implements and tests, human reviews
    authority: write code and tests
    approval_required: architecture changes, irreversible actions
    human_gate: review before merge

  L3 — Implement + Review + Fix
    description: AI implements, reviews, and fixes autonomously
    authority: full local development cycle
    approval_required: irreversible actions, high-risk decisions
    human_gate: final review on completion

  L4 — Autonomous Execution
    description: AI runs entire execution loop autonomously
    authority: execute full task lifecycle
    approval_required: irreversible actions, critical risk
    human_gate: escalation only

  L5 — Autonomous Multi-Task
    description: AI executes and coordinates multiple tasks
    authority: full autonomy across task portfolio
    approval_required: irreversible actions, security, critical risk
    human_gate: strategic oversight only

ProjectPolicy:

  declaration: @policy.autonomy
  format:
    <domain>:
      max: L<n>

  examples:
    @policy.autonomy
    payment:
      max: L2
    documentation:
      max: L4
    security:
      max: L1

  rules:
    [PA1] AI MUST read @policy.autonomy for the task's domain before
          starting.
    [PA2] AI MUST NOT exceed the max autonomy level for any domain.
    [PA3] If a task spans multiple domains, the LOWEST max applies
          (most restrictive wins).
    [PA4] Autonomy levels are per-domain — a task touching payment
          and docs uses min(payment=L2, documentation=L4) = L2.

ReversibleActions:

  definition: changes that can be undone without lasting impact
  examples:
    - rename local variable
    - refactor function
    - add test
    - add logging
    - update documentation
    - reorder imports
  rule: AI MAY perform reversible actions within the allowed autonomy level.

IrreversibleActions:

  definition: changes that cannot be undone without cost or risk
  examples:
    - delete data
    - change public API contract
    - database migration without rollback
    - security policy change
    - delete or rename a production entity
    - drop database column
  rule: AI MUST request human approval for ALL irreversible actions,
        regardless of autonomy level.

RiskLevelMapping:

  risk: low
    description: minimal impact if wrong
    autonomous_actions: full (within autonomy level)
    example: change README, add logging

  risk: medium
    description: moderate impact, reversible with effort
    autonomous_actions: yes, but review required on completion
    example: add new endpoint, refactor module

  risk: high
    description: significant impact, careful handling required
    autonomous_actions: no — approval required
    example: change payment algorithm, modify data schema

  risk: critical
    description: severe impact, requires human
    autonomous_actions: none — human required
    example: change authentication, delete production data

  rule: [RM1] Risk determines which review gates are activated.
  rule: [RM2] CRITICAL risk tasks MUST receive human approval before
          IN_PROGRESS.

AuthorityMatrix:

  | Autonomy | Reversible | Irreversible | Low Risk | Med Risk | High Risk | Critical Risk |
  |----------|------------|--------------|----------|----------|-----------|---------------|
  | L0       | observe    | none         | none     | none     | none      | none          |
  | L1       | propose    | propose      | propose  | propose  | propose   | propose       |
  | L2       | do         | propose      | do       | do+rev   | approve   | human         |
  | L3       | do         | propose      | do       | do+rev   | approve   | human         |
  | L4       | do         | propose      | do       | do       | approve   | human         |
  | L5       | do         | propose      | do       | do       | approve   | human         |

  Legend: observe = read only | propose = suggest only | do = execute |
          rev = review | approve = needs approval | human = needs human

Rules:

  [AP1] AI MUST NOT select its own autonomy level — it is set by policy.
  [AP2] AI MUST check both domain policy AND task risk before acting.
  [AP3] Irreversible actions ALWAYS require approval, regardless of level.
  [AP4] Critical risk ALWAYS requires human, regardless of level.
  [AP5] Autonomy level determines the depth of autonomous loop execution.
  [AP6] Domain policy overrides default task autonomy.
  [AP7] Escalating autonomy beyond project policy is a violation.

